items.note:
scripts/release/release-npm.sh [<version>] [--dry-run] works on bash 3.2 with set -euo pipefail and passes bash -n. The version defaults to package.json and must be X.Y.Z. Preflight checks, with no side effects:
- gh is signed in and has push access to the repo;
- the tag is absent locally and on GitHub (git ls-remote over HTTPS);
- npm returns 404 for vskill/$V;
- origin/main package.json, fetched over HTTPS, is at $V;
- CI on that SHA has not failed (in progress or absent is allowed).
It then tags the fetched SHA as a lightweight tag (v1.2.8 was lightweight too) and pushes refs/tags/v$V over HTTPS. If the push fails it deletes the local tag. It finds the npm Release run by --branch v$V plus headSha, retrying up to 120s, then runs `gh run watch --exit-status`. It polls registry.npmjs.org/vskill/$V for up to 300s, then runs `npx -y --prefer-online vskill@$V --version` from an empty temp dir and requires the output to contain $V. --dry-run stops before any tag or push. VSKILL_RELEASE_REMOTE overrides the remote, for rehearsing against a scratch clone.
